  Scenario: Error when required output validation framework is not provided
    Given the requirements specify a validation or equivalence framework
    When the PySpark code does not include the required validation logic
    Then the process must fail with error message "Missing required output validation framework"

  Scenario Outline: Data-driven test for supplier_invoice table write
    Given the PySpark DataFrame <df_name> with schema matching purgo_playground.supplier_invoice
    When writing the DataFrame to Unity Catalog table "purgo_playground.supplier_invoice" with partition key <partition_key> and format <table_format>
    Then the write operation must succeed
    And the table must contain all expected columns and data types
    And the partitioning must match <partition_key>
    And the compression must match <compression>
    Examples:
      | df_name                | partition_key | table_format | compression |
      | supplier_invoice_df    | invc_entry_dt | delta        | snappy      |
      | supplier_invoice_df    | fscl_yr_nbr   | parquet      | gzip        |

